3000
03:17:03,090 --> 03:17:05,270
Come on,

3001
03:17:11,420 --> 03:17:11,420
flowers.

3002
03:17:12,840 --> 03:17:13,380
Make it happen.

3003
03:17:15,440 --> 03:17:16,540
Oh, not this crap.

3004
03:17:22,050 --> 03:17:22,170
Yeah.

3005
03:17:31,650 --> 03:17:33,510
And then a fucking fly hits me.

3006
03:17:34,570 --> 03:17:35,730
Gotta be kidding me.

3007
03:17:37,170 --> 03:17:37,490
Stops for you.

3008
03:17:38,450 --> 03:17:38,950
Not that way.

3009
03:17:48,290 --> 03:17:48,870
Whoa!

3010
03:17:50,830 --> 03:17:52,750
That was a good run though.

3011
03:17:53,350 --> 03:17:54,010
That was nice.

3012
03:17:55,990 --> 03:17:56,730
Actually okay.

3013
03:17:57,030 --> 03:17:57,390
I don't mind.

3014
03:17:59,030 --> 03:17:59,830
Let's call it there.

3015
03:18:01,750 --> 03:18:03,250
That was actually amazing.

3016
03:18:03,850 --> 03:18:03,990
What?

3017
03:18:05,790 --> 03:18:07,090
This is some good runs.

3018
03:18:07,690 --> 03:18:07,930
Hold on.

3019
03:18:09,650 --> 03:18:10,750
I'm going to turn that down.

3020
03:18:12,170 --> 03:18:12,790
And turn this up.

3021
03:18:14,610 --> 03:18:15,710
It's fitting as hell.

3022
03:18:17,650 --> 03:18:18,310
Oh yeah.

3023
03:18:19,830 --> 03:18:20,930
What do you say to that, guys?

3024
03:18:22,230 --> 03:18:23,310
Did we win today or what?

3025
03:18:26,830 --> 03:18:28,130
Crazy dodging at the end, right?

3026
03:18:30,410 --> 03:18:32,630
Sometimes you're in a flow state and you're just like...

3027
03:18:34,530 --> 03:18:35,370
working out.

3028
03:18:38,960 --> 03:18:42,060
Killed mom again for like the fifth time in her fifth form or whatever.

3029
03:18:43,460 --> 03:18:45,320
I'm sure there's going to be more forms.

3030
03:18:48,360 --> 03:18:49,660
There's got to be a final form.

3031
03:18:52,790 --> 03:18:56,390
I love the complete 180 of you being set at the ending and then a strange door.

3032
03:18:56,810 --> 03:18:56,970
Yeah.

3033
03:18:57,690 --> 03:18:58,550
I'm glad it happened.

3034
03:18:59,690 --> 03:19:02,190
Because I was really down bad with the sadness, you know?

3035
03:19:03,310 --> 03:19:05,590
But then all of a sudden, I was down with the sickness.

3036
03:19:07,310 --> 03:19:08,510
A strange door, baby.

3037
03:19:10,770 --> 03:19:12,330
And boy did we find a strange door.

3038
03:19:12,470 --> 03:19:13,910
I haven't seen this door more strange than that.

3039
03:19:20,000 --> 03:19:22,660
44,857,475 forms.

3040
03:19:23,780 --> 03:19:24,540
You're lying.

3041
03:19:25,860 --> 03:19:26,440
That's not true.

3042
03:19:29,640 --> 03:19:31,540
Thank you for the Lazarus appreciation last week.

3043
03:19:32,000 --> 03:19:33,380
Lazarus is a cool guy, man.

3044
03:19:34,300 --> 03:19:36,700
He is an all around good character.

3045
03:19:37,500 --> 03:19:39,860
Solid HP, solid damage.

3046
03:19:40,060 --> 03:19:41,700
He's not like shitty in any ways.

3047
03:19:42,460 --> 03:19:43,760
He fucking comes back when he dies.

3048
03:19:44,160 --> 03:19:46,020
I mean, you got to love him.

3049
03:19:48,300 --> 03:19:49,120
Watch this music.

3050
03:19:51,280 --> 03:19:52,320
It is...

3051
03:19:54,640 --> 03:19:57,500
One of the most epic tracks in a video game sequence.

3052
03:19:57,640 --> 03:20:01,020
I'm not going to reveal what happens, of course, in that sequence, but...

3053
03:20:02,020 --> 03:20:02,800
Just play Ore.

3054
03:20:03,000 --> 03:20:03,800
It's a great game.

3055
03:20:07,280 --> 03:20:08,800
What do those scribbles on the screen mean?

3056
03:20:09,000 --> 03:20:09,240
I don't know.

3057
03:20:09,460 --> 03:20:10,540
Ask Edmond Macmillan.

3058
03:20:11,540 --> 03:20:12,600
He's the one who wrote them.

3059
03:20:14,520 --> 03:20:17,020
I wrote him a message and was like, Dude, I'm going to stream your game.

3060
03:20:17,200 --> 03:20:18,740
Do you mind making a background for me?

3061
03:20:18,760 --> 03:20:19,020
And he did.

3062
03:20:19,240 --> 03:20:20,380
He wrote this down for me.

3063
03:20:25,580 --> 03:20:27,000
I'm lying about that, by the way.

3064
03:20:27,680 --> 03:20:28,320
That's not true.

3065
03:20:29,920 --> 03:20:31,280
I don't have that kind of clout.

3066
03:20:35,950 --> 03:20:37,310
You unlocked and found so many things to stream.

3067
03:20:37,510 --> 03:20:40,030
I never played Isaac before, so it's fun unlocking things with you.

3068
03:20:40,250 --> 03:20:40,890
Hey, that's cool.

3069
03:20:41,770 --> 03:20:43,230
What do you think of the game so far, Gemini?

3070
03:20:44,450 --> 03:20:44,930
Or Gimini?

3071
03:20:46,490 --> 03:20:50,190
Or someone who hasn't played it before, but just watched me play it.

3072
03:20:51,270 --> 03:20:52,030
Is it confusing?

3073
03:20:52,330 --> 03:20:54,450
Do you understand what's happening on the screen, or...

3074
03:20:56,450 --> 03:20:57,430
Are you just going with the flow?

3075
03:20:59,130 --> 03:21:00,470
So did you like Jacob and Esau?

3076
03:21:00,590 --> 03:21:01,010
Yeah, I did.

3077
03:21:03,130 --> 03:21:04,830
He turned into my favorite character.

3078
03:21:08,220 --> 03:21:13,440
It's kind of funny that the boss title from yesterday was...

3079
03:21:13,440 --> 03:21:18,260
This is my new favorite character, which is, of course, the Apollyon character, right?

3080
03:21:19,040 --> 03:21:23,040
And then today I get a character where I turn into him.

3081
03:21:23,180 --> 03:21:24,300
So the title's going to be...

3082
03:21:24,920 --> 03:21:26,200
This is my new favorite characters.

3083
03:21:26,660 --> 03:21:27,300
Or these are.

3084
03:21:28,400 --> 03:21:29,720
It's just the same character.

3085
03:21:31,440 --> 03:21:33,820
Or this is still my favorite characters.

3086
03:21:35,660 --> 03:21:36,480
I love that.

3087
03:21:40,870 --> 03:21:42,070
That's the best title, right?

3088
03:21:42,270 --> 03:21:42,530
Isn't it?

3089
03:21:42,670 --> 03:21:43,170
I feel like that's...

3090
03:21:43,710 --> 03:21:45,450
Sometimes you just have the perfect title in mind.

3091
03:21:50,050 --> 03:21:52,550
If you want that Apollyon run, you would have made some people very rich.

3092
03:21:52,690 --> 03:21:54,990
Since everyone voted you would lose with Jacob and Esau.

3093
03:21:55,150 --> 03:21:56,390
Oh, that's funny.

3094
03:21:57,490 --> 03:21:58,610
That is actually hilarious.

3095
03:22:01,800 --> 03:22:04,680
Is this my first loss to Hush, by the way?

3096
03:22:05,620 --> 03:22:08,020
I feel like I've been slapping that guy left and right.

3097
03:22:08,120 --> 03:22:09,940
But now, finally, it was my time to get slapped.

3098
03:22:13,120 --> 03:22:13,440
Amazing.

3099
03:22:15,960 --> 03:22:18,460
I don't think I've ever lost to... No, that's not true.

3100
03:22:18,540 --> 03:22:20,520
I was about to say Delirium, but I have lost to that guy.

3101
03:22:22,300 --> 03:22:25,460
It is the Hush one that I have been doing well against.

3102
03:22:28,360 --> 03:22:30,020
It was so pock when you figured out the mirror.

3103
03:22:30,360 --> 03:22:32,200
It will be even more pock next to figure out whatever.

3104
03:22:33,020 --> 03:22:34,740
Dude, I feel so stupid in hindsight because...

3105
03:22:35,760 --> 03:22:37,540
Obviously there was something with that mirror, right?

3106
03:22:37,640 --> 03:22:39,500
Because it was on the map and it was very...

3107
03:22:39,500 --> 03:22:41,840
It was on every single time I was there, the mirror was there.

3108
03:22:42,740 --> 03:22:48,140
I should have just asked myself the question, what can I actually do on this floor, you know?

3109
03:22:48,940 --> 03:22:51,680
And obviously the fire was one of the things that are different.

3110
03:22:53,040 --> 03:22:54,620
So I should have realized that earlier.

3111
03:22:56,100 --> 03:22:57,940
But I'm glad I figured it out.

3112
03:22:59,580 --> 03:23:03,520
Minus seven luck must be... I mean, I thought for sure it was a trade-off, you know?

3113
03:23:04,140 --> 03:23:06,100
That was an interaction, a genuine interaction.

3114
03:23:06,320 --> 03:23:07,920
You blow up the mirror and something happens.

3115
03:23:08,520 --> 03:23:11,500
The game responds by showing you a destroyed mirror.

3116
03:23:12,740 --> 03:23:12,900
Minus seven luck?

3117
03:23:13,800 --> 03:23:15,400
Surely that could have been something there.

3118
03:23:17,280 --> 03:23:18,180
Like a trade-off, right?

3119
03:23:18,860 --> 03:23:20,280
A trade-off that I didn't know what was.

3120
03:23:24,640 --> 03:23:26,780
Oliver, didn't you know ghosts can travel through mirrors in real life?

3121
03:23:26,900 --> 03:23:27,700
I did not know that.

3122
03:23:27,800 --> 03:23:29,180
I don't believe in ghosts.

3123
03:23:30,560 --> 03:23:31,780
So therefore my eyes aren't real.

3124
03:23:34,800 --> 03:23:36,920
Dude, Jaden Smith would love downpour.

3125
03:23:38,160 --> 03:23:38,720
Am I right?

3126
03:23:42,790 --> 03:23:44,690
The mother ending cutscene was so sad.

3127
03:23:44,870 --> 03:23:46,430
Dude, I was actually crying a little bit.

3128
03:23:47,370 --> 03:23:48,270
I was shedding a manly tear.

3129
03:23:50,250 --> 03:23:50,930
Who am I kidding?

3130
03:23:51,130 --> 03:23:52,070
I shed a normal tear.

3131
03:23:54,210 --> 03:23:55,250
That was sad as hell.

3132
03:24:04,270 --> 03:24:05,210
I think so, Giminy.

3133
03:24:06,890 --> 03:24:08,530
I think it's the first time we heard his voice.

3134
03:24:08,650 --> 03:24:11,650
I was about to comment on it, but then I got absorbed in the cutscene.

3135
03:24:12,470 --> 03:24:14,230
I was like taking it back when I heard his voice.

3136
03:24:14,370 --> 03:24:14,930
I was like, what?

3137
03:24:15,790 --> 03:24:15,990
You know?

3138
03:24:20,820 --> 03:24:21,720
Do you believe in mirrors?

3139
03:24:21,820 --> 03:24:22,660
I don't.

3140
03:24:24,120 --> 03:24:25,700
They don't really show reality.

3141
03:24:27,460 --> 03:24:28,100
It's fake.

3142
03:24:31,610 --> 03:24:32,930
Should we watch the starting cutscene?

3143
03:24:33,030 --> 03:24:33,910
I should actually.

3144
03:24:35,170 --> 03:24:35,930
That's a good point.

3145
03:24:38,810 --> 03:24:39,570
Okay, I gotta go.

3146
03:24:39,770 --> 03:24:41,270
Jackie is murdering me for food.

3147
03:24:41,750 --> 03:24:44,130
Even though it's technically in 15 minutes, she needs to be fed.

3148
03:24:45,150 --> 03:24:47,610
Guys, I'm gonna go to my parents tomorrow and be there for a couple days.

3149
03:24:47,810 --> 03:24:49,150
So no streams for the next couple days.

3150
03:24:49,930 --> 03:24:51,230
After that, we're back to Isaac.

3151
03:24:51,910 --> 03:24:54,890
I'm gonna try and keep the excitement contained within me.

3152
03:24:55,570 --> 03:24:58,750
So yeah, my father has a birthday.

3153
03:25:00,110 --> 03:25:01,430
So we gotta go celebrate that.

3154
03:25:02,530 --> 03:25:04,730
Thanks for watching everyone, and I'll see you around!

3155
03:25:05,810 --> 03:25:06,590
Enjoy your day.

3156
03:25:07,510 --> 03:25:09,030
Next time we will win even more.

3157
03:25:10,770 --> 03:25:11,450
Bye-bye.
